    "title": "Is the stock market closed on Good Friday?",
    "text": "April 3, 2026, 8:06 a.m. ETGood Friday is not a federal holiday in Rhode Island or the rest of the United States, but it is a public holiday for some states and there will be lots of closed businesses and services, including the stock market.The Nasdaq and the New York Stock Exchange will be closed on Good Friday, but most banks will be open for regular business hours. Many schools are off for Good Friday and the Easter weekend break.Good Friday commemorates the crucifixion of Jesus Christ, which according to Christian belief, is seen as a sacrifice that atones for the sins of humanity. While the day is a somber one, it is also considered \"good\" because it leads to the hope and joy of Easter Sunday where the resurrection of Jesus is celebrated, signifying victory over death.What is closed on Good Friday?Although it's not a federally observed holiday in the U.S., Good Friday is recognized as a state public holiday in states such as Delaware and New Jersey. However, Rhode Island is not one of those states.Most major retailers and restaurants are expected to be open for business as usual.The U.S. Postal Service facilities will have normal operations and mail will be delivered as usual, as will UPS and FedEx services.Good Friday falls on April 3 this year during Holy Week, which started with Palm Sunday on March 29, 2026 and ends with Easter Sunday. This year's Passover week (April 1-9) overlaps with Holy Week.Unlike many other holidays, the Easter holiday dates change every year. It can be as early as March 22 or as late as April 25, which means the Lenten period and Good Friday also change.",
